# DIBAY Existing-Live Schema Authority

**ADOPTED.** Full contract: `docs/dibay-existing-live-schema-authority-convention.md`

## When it applies

Live table exists **and** repo CREATE authority is missing → use this convention only.

## Outcomes

| Result | Action |
|---|---|
| MATCH | NO-OP / PASS |
| DRIFT / EXTRA | FAIL-FAST — no auto-fix |
| MISSING table | BLOCK — no auto-CREATE on recovery path |

**ASSERT BEFORE MUTATE.** Recovery ≠ Creation ≠ Repair.

## DO NOT

- Close authority with `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` alone
- Silent catch-up `ALTER` / policy/index “repair” as recovery
- DDL inside recovery fingerprints or `verify:schema-authority`
- Invent ORM/DSL/new DB framework for this
- Expand beyond TABLE SCHEMA AUTHORITY without Owner decision

## Expected form

Versioned JSON under:

`supabase/schema-authority/<schema>/<table>/v<N>.fingerprint.json`

Canonical check (when implemented): `scripts/verify-schema-authority.mjs` (read-only catalog).

## Payment note

`store_payments` / `store_payment_events` use this global convention — not a one-off exception.
